SUMMARY:Monthly Club Meeting – “Wearables for Wildlife: Behind the Scen
 es with the Evolution of Wildlife Telemetry Technologies”
DESCRIPTION:Club Meeting – North Museum of Nature and Science\, 400 Colle
 ge Ave\, Lancaster\, PA 17603 Presented by Club President Andy McGann Andy
  McGann grew up birding in Southcentral Pennsylvania and his early experie
 nces ultimately led to a career in the field of Movement Ecology. His time
  in academia\, non-profits\, consulting\, and ultimately to a wildlife tel
 emetry tech company spanned a timeframe that saw the science advance from 
 analog radio telemetry to “smart devices” with GPS\, accelerometers\, 
 and global Internet connectivity. In his career\, Andy combined his experi
 ences in ornithology with his love of technology and appreciation for geog
 raphy in order to help wildlife researchers and organizations around the w
 orld obtain the scientific information needed to help conserve some of the
  rarest birds we have left. Andy will discuss the evolution of the technol
 ogy\, the current state-of-the-art\, and paint a picture of where we are g
 oing.\n\nPrice: Not supplied by this calendar\; check event details\n\nSch
 edule listed: Thu\, Dec 10\, 2026 07:00 PM EST – Thu\, Dec 10\, 2026 08:
 30 PM EST\n\nSchedule supplied by Lancaster County Bird Club\n\nTimes conv
 erted from America/New_York to UTC for calendar compatibility.\n\n\n\nRegi
